==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|LL.}} {{term|recapitulus}}, past participle of {{term|recapitulare||to go over the main points of a thing again}} < {{etyl|la}} {{term|re-||again}} + {{term|capitulum||a head, main part, chapter}}; see [[capitulate]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Canada|UK}} {{IPA|/riːkəˈpɪtʃʊleɪt/}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|recapitulat|ing}}

# to [[summarize]] or repeat in concise form
#: ''The entire [[symphony]] was '''recapitulated''' in the last four [[bars]].''
# to repeat the evolutionary stages of an organism during its embryonic development
#: ''[[ontogeny|Ontogeny]] '''recapitulates''' [[phylogeny]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to summarize or repeat in concise form}} [[recap]], [[sum up]]

